 """
+    gw_action_losses(power_coefficients, coupling_to_hole, frequencies, actions, mass)
+
+Quanta lost per unit `τ` by each bound mode to gravitational-wave annihilation
+(two quanta of the same mode become one graviton, which leaves to infinity),
+in reference units. A mode with wave action `N_i` and real frequency `ω_i` is
+treated as a cloud of mass `M_cloud,i / M₀ = κ ω_i N_i`, with
+`κ = (f_a/M_Pl)²` (`coupling_to_hole`). It radiates the power
+`P_i = c_i (M_cloud,i / M)²`, where `c_i` is the mode's entry of
+`power_coefficients` and `M = b M₀` (`mass` is `b`). Losing the energy `P_i`
+means losing quanta at the rate `P_i / (κ ω_i) = c_i κ ω_i N_i² / b²`.
+
+The coefficients are computed for the linear bound state, so this is accurate
+only where the field is small in units of `f_a`.
+"""
+gw_action_losses(power_coefficients, coupling_to_hole, frequencies, actions, mass) =
+    power_coefficients .* coupling_to_hole .* frequencies .* actions .^ 2 ./ mass^2
+
